# starlight-versions writes frozen snapshots of prior major docs under
# website/src/content/docs/<major>/ (e.g. 2.0/) plus a versions/*.json sidebar
# snapshot. These are generated plugin output, not hand-authored — leave them
# exactly as emitted instead of reformatting them.
website/src/content/docs/[0-9]*/**
website/src/content/versions/*.json

# Starlight content markdown is exempt from prettier entirely.
#
# `proseWrap: always` re-wraps prose across line boundaries, which breaks remark
# directives: a `:::caution` aside whose closing `:::` gets pulled onto the
# preceding content line stops terminating the directive and renders as literal
# text on the published page. Neither `check:docs` nor `docs:build` catches it —
# it is only visible in the built HTML. This bit issue #33 (a stray `:::` shipped
# live in reference/errors.md) and again in #34, and the workaround was to sprinkle
# `<!-- prettier-ignore -->` above every aside, which is easy to forget and easy to
# get wrong. Formatting authored docs is not worth a class of silent rendering bugs.
#
# Two `<!-- prettier-ignore -->` markers remain in the content (queries.md,
# errors.md); they are now no-ops and can be dropped at any time.
#
# Code, config, ADRs under docs/, and the repo READMEs are still prettier-formatted.
website/**/*.md
website/**/*.mdx
